**Read progressively:** [Modules in Mechanics of Materials — David Roylance](../../mechanical-engineering-and-machine-design/sources/Mechanics-of-Materials-Roylance.lingua#r_7K2RYA9504FGFGJTVWHMWXD5WY), the complete material-response, constitutive, viscoelastic, yield and fracture modules with problems; [Applied Mechanics of Solids — Allan F. Bower](../../mechanical-engineering-and-machine-design/sources/Applied-Mechanics-of-Solids-Bower.lingua#r_109WFZBWMEMGHV9TGFD22H2F1W), chapters 2–3 and 9 with their mathematical appendices as needed. Work the full published [Mechanical Behavior of Materials — Krystyn Van Vliet, MIT 3.22](../../../materials/metals-and-metallurgical-production/sources/Mechanical-Behavior-MIT-3-22.lingua#r_53J3ZM414SJR3SFW7Q1G8ZJWDC) graduate progression, using the open books for fuller derivations where its required commercial text is unavailable. Read the family-specific sequences below alongside these mechanics sources.

The same composition can acquire very different behavior through structure, processing, temperature, moisture, loading rate and damage. A property is an answer to a specified experiment, not merely a number beside a material name. Start with a metal fastener, a ceramic insulator, a polymer seal and a layered panel. Describe the functions and observations before choosing equations.

**Work:** For each object identify structure, load path, environment, timescale and a plausible failure mechanism. Distinguish an intrinsic mechanism, a homogenized constitutive description, a measured specimen response and whole-component performance. Through this section, produce three substantial studies that compare predictions with evidence, rather than treating a catalogue of material families as mastery.

**Return:** [Materials engineering — structure, processing and useful behavior](../Materials-engineering.lingua#r_05BF5JM8141RKF1VT5998YFZQ9).
**Continue in materials engineering:** [Compare metal and alloy states with evidence](../families/Compare-metal-and-alloy-states-with-evidence.lingua#r_1MRASEY87AB97C5WP159FCTDTA).

